*  STONE_driver - drives stone.spt, which plays a game of taking stones from a
*  pile through the published function SDA(NSTONES,PARITY,MAX).  Contract per
*  stone.spt header.  STONE carries its own END, so a driver can only be the
*  include; the fixture stone_driver.in supplies the moves.  The form finds
*  phrases.in under its lower-case name and then plays a whole game on standard
*  input (INPUT(.INPUT,5,' -f0')): the fixture's moves run out and sbl -bf asks
*  again forever (OUTSIDE_SPITBOL_BASELINE.tsv).  Owed: moves that play the game
*  to its end (UNGRADED.tsv, NEEDS_STDIN_FIXTURE).
-INCLUDE "stone.spt"
